Playing NH 3.0j+ on the Mac, in wizard mode, I noticed that if you have
the spell "teleport away" memorized and then try to teleport with ctrl-T,
the game thinks you are using the spell to teleport, and gives you the
"You can barely remeber the runes of this spell" message, etc., before
you teleport. Oddly, even after the spell is used up, you get the message,
but you can still teleport.

I think that this bug may be limited to wizard mode, since in my last 
(winning) game, my high[A-level priest also had tport memorized, yet could
use ctrl-T without difficulty.

Also, someone mentioned the game going into disorder when throwing an
unpaid gem at a unicorn in a shop. I was unable to reproduce this
phenomenon. My game correctly interpreted this act -- when I tported out
of the shop, the Ko[Z_tps came running.

